      players: 'One player. Plait is a solo patience game played by a single person; BVS and historical sources describe it as a single-player card game with no opponents or partners.',
      deck: '104 cards (two standard 52-card decks).',
      equipment: '104 cards (two standard 52-card decks).',
      dealing: 'Deal 13 cards in a plait (open reserve). Deal 32 cards into 8 tableau piles (4 cards per pile). Place one card above as the first foundation base; the seven other cards of the same rank become foundation bases as they appear. Remainder is stock.',
